{
  "rationale": "Evidence from the last race (entityR2A, iteration 1 candidate, 60 trials): the oval finished in 19 of 20 trials at a mean time of 1.88 s, so the 1.2 base_speed and the wider sensor spread are workable on gentle curves. The s-bend and slalom failed in every trial (0 of 40 finished), with progress of 0.39 and 0.17, about one line-loss event per run, and max_error of 0.062 to 0.064 m, at or just past the 0.06 m off-track limit. steering_oscillation was 0.21 on every track, above the 0.15 level the feedback flags as overcorrection. The robot is therefore swinging across the line on the sharper bends, losing the tape and not recovering. The Evaluator's rule for high oscillation with max_error near the limit is to lower kp or raise kd. I am doing both, moderately: kp 1.2 to 1.0 reduces the turn gain on a full-scale signal from about 840 to about 700 PWM, and kd 0.3 to 0.4 damps the change in signal that drives the jitter. Geometry is held fixed, as the Evaluator asked, so the controller is tuned on the ±0.032 m, 16 mm sensor spread before any geometry change. base_speed stays at 1.2 because the oval shows time margin (1.88 s against the 3 s limit) and a slower entry into bends should help the sharp sections. sensor_weights and line_loss ('last_direction') are unchanged, so the only edits are kp and kd. Expected result: steering_oscillation falls below about 0.15, max_error on the s-bend and slalom stays under 0.06 m, line_loss_events drops toward 0 on those tracks, and the s-bend and slalom finish or reach much higher progress, with the oval still finishing. Hypotheses to check next: (1) if oscillation falls but line_loss persists with max_error still near 0.06 m, kp is now too low for the tight bends, so raise kp to about 1.2 to 1.3 with kd at 0.4; (2) if oscillation stays above 0.15, raise kd toward 0.5 before lowering kp further; (3) if the robot finishes with completion_time above 3 s, raise base_speed toward 1.5 with kp and kd fixed. Measurements requested: completion, progress, completion_time, rms_error, max_error, line_loss_events and steering_oscillation, per track.",
  "geometry": {
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "mass": 0.8,
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.032, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.016, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.016, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.032, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.016,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "wheel_track": 0.12
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.2,
    "kp": 1.0,
    "ki": 0.0,
    "kd": 0.4,
    "sensor_weights": [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Damped steering, kp 1.0",
      "notes": "Lowers kp from 1.2 to 1.0 and raises kd from 0.3 to 0.4, with geometry and base_speed unchanged. The last race showed oscillation of 0.21 with max_error at the 0.06 m limit on the s-bend and slalom, and all 40 trials there went off track. The oval finished 19 of 20 trials, so the fix targets only the bends."
    }
  }
}
